    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "specifically for things on a national level. We saw them come true. We saw the hand of favor of the Lord. Last year at Regent University, we instituted this through Roberts and School of Government. And so we had people join us literally from all over the world, from Australia, from different countries. Because it was during COVID, people needed to have this fellowship. Now that we're somewhat past COVID, people still are desperate for the fellowship. And I think particularly as we look at where the United States is at, but as we look at where the world is at, we're not the only one suffering across the world. People are suffering because of the absolutely insane political decisions made by various political leaders. And so it isn't just our economy that's suffering, it's other economies. Germany is in crisis right now with energy. The United Kingdom is in crisis right now. People will be spending 20% of their income, 20% just to pay a fuel bill so they don't freeze this winter in the United Kingdom. So as we look at all these things, according to God's calendar, this is the time for us to come before Him. It's like the first fruits in a way. This is our time to go to Him, bow down. The Jewish New Year is called Rosh Hashanah. And so during that particular time, We need to set our year right. And I know I've seen it my own life that my whole year was changed by giving this time to the Lord, seeking his face to hear his voice and to beseech him, maybe on behalf of our family, our nation,",
